00:05:49.245 --> 00:05:51.475
and I pull out my flip phone

00:05:51.475 --> 00:05:52.965
because that's what we had back then.

00:05:52.965 --> 00:05:53.798
- [Gary] I remember.
- And I call my dad

00:05:53.798 --> 00:05:55.683
- [Gary] Good job.
- Because I felt so guilty

00:05:55.683 --> 00:05:57.670
I didn't want to disrespect my parents

00:05:57.670 --> 00:05:58.994
and quit this job
- [Gary] Good for you.

00:05:58.994 --> 00:05:59.827
when I don't have any other way

00:05:59.827 --> 00:06:01.493
- [Gary] Understood.
- to make a living.

00:06:01.493 --> 00:06:02.654
And I was certainly not
going to go back home.

00:06:02.654 --> 00:06:04.265
And my dad told me one of
the most important things

00:06:04.265 --> 00:06:05.098
I've ever heard.

00:06:05.098 --> 00:06:05.931
He said, "Look.

00:06:05.931 --> 00:06:07.332
"You've worked since
you were nine years old.

00:06:07.332 --> 00:06:08.440
"I am not worried about you

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:09.448
"keeping a roof over your head

00:06:09.448 --> 00:06:10.709
"or putting food on the table.

00:06:10.709 --> 00:06:11.982
"but you are going to work for the next

00:06:11.982 --> 00:06:13.516
"40-50 years at least.

00:06:13.516 --> 00:06:14.987
"If you don't find something

00:06:14.987 --> 00:06:17.109
"that you love so much,

00:06:17.109 --> 00:06:18.274
"you're going to be miserable."

00:06:18.274 --> 00:06:19.217
- [Gary] Good.

00:06:19.217 --> 00:06:20.050
- "So quit this job.

00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:21.420
"Take as long as you
need to find that thing

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:22.918
